            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0345" n="280" xml:id="pg280"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4949: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-13T17:00:00-04:00">August 13, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. Your 508, August 4, 9 a.m. The Paris Embassy reports that the matter was
                    taken up with the Foreign Office on August 8 and that the Foreign Office has now
                    replied that they are at a loss to understand why the shipment was held up and
                    that the Ministry of Colonies has been requested to telegraph the necessary
                    instructions to the Governor of French Somaliland for the forwarding of the
                    shipment to you.</p>
                <p>Please keep the Department promptly informed of developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
